---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHeader from "../components/PageHeader.astro";
import Section from "../components/Section.astro";
import { withBase } from "../lib/paths";
import { SPEC_HREF as specHref, NEW_TAB, isExternal } from "../lib/links";

const asks = [
  "Writing, reading, or both, a zip file containing passport.json and its media files, conforming to the published schema.",
  "Ignoring fields your system does not recognize, so that newer files never cause your reader to fail.",
  "Retaining each record's originRef on import and exporting it unchanged, so that records keep their identity across a series of transfers.",
  "Following the versioning rules in the specification.",
];

const neverAsks = [
  "Sharing data with anyone other than the receiving facility. Animal Passport is a file format, not a data network.",
  "Paying fees or entering into an agreement.",
  "Implementing every record type. Export the types your system holds and import the types it can store.",
  "Connecting to any external service, or depending on any one company's governance.",
];

const resources = [
  { title: "The specification", body: "Developed publicly on GitHub, where the specification text, the JSON Schema and the sample passports are published.", href: specHref, link: "github.com/animal-passport/spec" },
  { title: "Sample passports", body: "Two fictitious animals, a harbor seal and her dam, that together include every field defined in version 0.1.", href: withBase("/examples/pebble.json"), link: "Download Pebble's passport.json" },
  { title: "The passport viewer", body: "Displays any passport in a web browser, including fields it does not recognize, which makes it a quick check of what your export produces.", href: withBase("/viewer"), link: "Open the viewer" },
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title="For software vendors — Animal Passport"
  description="For developers of animal records software: one open format to export and import, in place of a custom integration with every other system. What implementation requires, and what it does not."
>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="For software vendors"
    title="One format in place of every custom integration"
    lede="Your customers are required to meet AZA standard 1.4.12, and they need complete records for every animal they receive. Animal Passport is an open format for both: implement it once, and your system can exchange records with any other system that does the same."
  />

  <Section narrow flushTop>
    <div class="space-y-5 text-navy-700 text-[1.075rem] leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        At present, moving an animal's records between two systems requires either a custom integration for that pair of systems or a set of PDF exports. Neither scales, and no vendor can resolve this alone, because a format read by only one system does not serve as a shared standard. A useful format is one that every system in the field can write and read, from the largest networks to in-house databases.
      </p>
      <p>
        Version 0.1 is based on real data. It covers medical, husbandry, welfare, training and transaction records in detail, and its rules were developed by exporting and re-importing complete animal histories. We particularly want to hear where it does not fit your data model.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section background="cream-100" eyebrow="Implementation" heading="What implementation requires, and what it does not">
    <div class="grid gap-10 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div>
        <h3 class="font-serif text-xl font-medium text-navy-900" style="font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 14;">
          Required
        </h3>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-navy-700 leading-relaxed">
          {asks.map((a) => (
            <li class="flex gap-3">
              <span class="text-teal-700 font-bold mt-1" aria-hidden="true">✓</span>
              <span>{a}</span>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="font-serif text-xl font-medium text-navy-900" style="font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 14;">
          Not required
        </h3>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-navy-700 leading-relaxed">
          {neverAsks.map((a) => (
            <li class="flex gap-3">
              <span class="text-muted-500 mt-1" aria-hidden="true">—</span>
              <span>{a}</span>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section eyebrow="Resources" heading="Available now">
    <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-3">
      {resources.map((r) => (
        <article>
          <h3 class="font-serif text-xl font-medium text-navy-900" style="font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 14;">
            {r.title}
          </h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-navy-700 leading-relaxed">{r.body}</p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            <a href={r.href} {...(isExternal(r.href) ? NEW_TAB : {})} class="link font-medium">{r.link} →</a>
          </p>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p class="mt-10 text-navy-700 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl">
      How the format is governed, and how stewardship is intended to pass to an independent body, is described on the <a href={withBase("/about")} class="link font-medium">About</a> page.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section background="teal-50" narrow>
    <div class="text-center">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-navy-900 text-[clamp(1.6rem,3vw,2rem)] tracking-tight" style="font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 32;">
        Review it against your own data
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-navy-700 leading-relaxed max-w-xl mx-auto">
        The most valuable review comes from people who know a different records system. Tell us where version 0.1 does not fit yours.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-3">
        <a href={withBase("/contact?role=vendor")} class="w-full sm:w-auto text-center rounded-full bg-teal-700 text-cream-50 px-6 py-3 font-medium hover:bg-teal-600 transition-colors">Contact us</a>
        <a href={specHref} {...NEW_TAB} class="w-full sm:w-auto text-center rounded-full border border-teal-700 text-teal-700 px-6 py-3 font-medium hover:bg-cream-50 transition-colors">Specification on GitHub</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>
